/*
Title: Apache encoded path traversal investigation
Status: Validated as an investigation query in the CSEC 5350 lab
Data source: Apache access events forwarded through rsyslog and Logstash
Purpose: Identify requests containing traversal or shell-oriented indicators
*/

program:"apache_access"
AND message:("/cgi-bin" OR "%2e" OR "bin/sh" OR "etc/passwd")

/*
Higher-context variant when the parsed status field is available:

program:"apache_access"
AND http.response.status_code:(400 OR 403)
AND url.path:("/cgi-bin" OR *"%2e"* OR *"bin/sh"* OR *"etc/passwd"*)


Validation notes:
- Detected the controlled GET and POST requests in the completed exercise.
- HTTP 400/403 indicates rejection, not proof that a request was harmless.
- Tune field names to the deployed Logstash parsing schema.
- Add source aggregation and a time window before promoting to an alert.
*/
